." Manpage for smi-agent-cli-options
.TH smi-agent-cli-options 1 "September 2026" "setmy.info" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
smi-agent-cli-options \- print agent specific model and reasoning options
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smi-agent-cli-options
.I AGENT
.RB [ \-\-model
.IR MODEL ]
.RB [ \-\-reasoning
.IR LEVEL ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B smi-agent-cli-options
command translates the generic
.B \-\-model
and
.B \-\-reasoning
options into the flags of one agent CLI and prints them on one line, ready to append to a
.BR smi-agent-cli (1)
call:
.PP
.RS
.B AGENT_CLI_OPTIONS=$(smi-agent-cli-options claude --model sonnet --reasoning high)
.br
.B smi-agent-cli claude TASKLIST.sexp ${AGENT_CLI_OPTIONS}
.RE
.PP
Without
.B \-\-model
the first, least expensive, entry of the agent's model list is used; without
.B \-\-reasoning
the level is
.BR low .
The model is validated against the agent's model list, the level against
.BR "low medium high" .
Model lists and the option mapping live in one place,
.IR ai-agents.sh ,
one function per agent.
.SH MAPPING
.TP
.BR claude ", " agy
.B --model
.I MODEL
.B --effort
.I LEVEL
.TP
.B codex
.B --model
.I MODEL
.B -c model_reasoning_effort=\c
.I LEVEL
.TP
.BR cursor ", " codewhale ", " opencode
.B --model
.I MODEL
\(em the reasoning level is ignored.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 1
Missing agent name, unknown agent, unknown model, unknown reasoning level, or unknown option.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
.B $ smi-agent-cli-options claude
.br
--model haiku --effort low
.br
.B $ smi-agent-cli-options codex --model gpt-5.1 --reasoning medium
.br
--model gpt-5.1 -c model_reasoning_effort=medium
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smi-agent (1),
.BR smi-agent-cli (1)
